---
export const prerender = true;
import MarketingLayout from "../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro";
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | CrawlPact"
  description="What data CrawlPact collects, why, how long it is retained, and the third parties involved in operating the service."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-reading px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-h1 text-neutral-950">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-supporting text-neutral-500">
      Draft — not yet reviewed by a lawyer. This page describes CrawlPact's actual technical data
      practices as implemented.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">What CrawlPact collects</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">CrawlPact stores only information required for:</p>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-5 text-body text-neutral-700">
      <li>Your account (a display name and passkey credentials — no password, no email address)</li>
      <li>
        Billing, limited to identifiers needed to link your account to a Paddle customer and
        subscription
      </li>
      <li>
        Domains you save, and bounded snapshots of the public policy resources CrawlPact scanned for
        them
      </li>
      <li>Security logs needed to detect abuse</li>
      <li>First-party product-usage events (see below)</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      CrawlPact does not store copies of entire websites — only the specific, bounded resources
      relevant to AI crawler policy (e.g. <code>robots.txt</code>, <code>llms.txt</code>, relevant
      headers).
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">Third parties</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      Cloudflare provides hosting, storage (D1), and scheduled execution. Paddle is CrawlPact's
      merchant of record for billing and independently sends payment-related communications. Google
      Analytics is used on public marketing pages (this page, the homepage, pricing, and similar
      pages) to measure visits; it is not loaded on the authenticated app or admin areas. CrawlPact
      does not use any third-party email, SMS, push-notification, AI API, or external authentication
      provider.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">Retention</h2>
    <table class="mt-4 w-full border-collapse text-left text-body">
      <thead>
        <tr class="border-b border-neutral-200 text-supporting font-medium text-neutral-600">
          <th scope="col" class="py-2">Data</th>
          <th scope="col" class="py-2">Retention</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="divide-y divide-neutral-100">
        <tr
          ><td class="py-2 text-neutral-800">Anonymous scan cache</td><td
            class="py-2 text-neutral-900">24 hours to 7 days</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td class="py-2 text-neutral-800">Free account scan history</td><td
            class="py-2 text-neutral-900">30 days</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td class="py-2 text-neutral-800">Solo plan history</td><td class="py-2 text-neutral-900"
            >12 months</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td class="py-2 text-neutral-800">Pro plan history</td><td class="py-2 text-neutral-900"
            >24 months</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td class="py-2 text-neutral-800">Agency plan history</td><td
            class="py-2 text-neutral-900">36 months</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td class="py-2 text-neutral-800">Deleted account private data</td><td
            class="py-2 text-neutral-900">Purged within 30 days where permitted</td
          ></tr
        >
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">Your rights</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      You can request account deletion at any time from account settings. Deletion begins a
      cancellable grace period, after which private data is purged where permitted (billing records
      required for legal/tax purposes are retained separately — see the retention table above).
    </p>
  </article>
</MarketingLayout>
